\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Twelve massive man-made leech lakes tiled Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s large estate, each a perfect square. The rim of the nearest squares were lined with roofless stalls, with each stall penning a live animal into the shallows. Goats, horses, cows; any animal larger than a large dog would do. They were each slumped onto support beams. Their snouts were tied into bags of intoxicating freeweed smoke. This was not an act of beneficence to inure them to the pain, it was Vigram\u8217\'92s way of keeping his peaceful country air free of their horrible moaning.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The rest of the estate was mostly flies and marshgrass. The sky was cloudy with the kind of tall, mountainous clouds that swallowed landscape paintings whole, the kind that cast broad shadows down upon the world to pull the viewer through the distance, as they pulled Mandri now, all the way out to the sparkling blue line on the horizon which was the sea.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram set himself to work in setting up an easel which he claimed to have built himself. Slaves cut and planed the lumber, brewed the glue, hammered the metal fittings, but Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s mighty mind designed it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you sure you want to do this here?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked as he paced about the vine-trellised, brown brick patio.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not here?\u8221\'94 said Vigram.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri eyed the distressed animals in the lakes below. Shaved down to the pink skin like criminals, they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d been reduced to bags of blood. Leechmen waded between the stalls so that they could trowel off the largest leeches and toss them into grass baskets. Those leeches which weren\u8217\'92t engaged in the constant struggle for the cleanest spot of flesh were busy rippling the water\u8217\'92s surface with their mating. It was a bit of an orgy down there. If only those foul creatures knew that their bliss came at a cost.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s stomach turned. On came a pang of guilt, because all those goats, horses, and cows were suffering in leech paradise on account of him. He\u8217\'92d eaten more than his fill of Meskalimi leech. Who was he to judge Vigram\u8217\'92s trade? What right did he have to feel compassion for those animals when his own stomach was full of leech?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well,\u8221\'94 Mandri said as he eyed the patio\u8217\'92s trellis. \u8220\'93These vines aren\u8217\'92t yet thick enough for a solid shadow. A dappled light will fall upon the sitter. It\u8217\'92s going to make things difficult.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He moved into the dappled shade to demonstrate the effect on his own skin.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93My dear Mandriiii,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, his drawl rolling heavily. \u8220\'93The patterns of light and shadow are a magical vesture.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well,\u8221\'94 Mandri pondered, \u8220\'93I might suggest that you worry about \u8216\'91magical vestures\u8217\'92 when you\u8217\'92re skilled enough to make a face look like a face.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No,\u8221\'94 Vigram said firmly, long beard wiggling. \u8220\'93I won\u8217\'92t have it any other way. A magical vesture for a magical subject.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 As if bidden from the heavens by Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s words, a woman joined them on the patio. Younger than Vigram, older than Mandri, this unfamiliar beauty was tall, thin, with clear brown skin, sun-kissed cheeks, and long brown hair falling over her shoulder. Her austere green eyes stared down a thin nose that was impossible to reason with. In a word: perfection. Altogether, she was something like a tree. Mandri supposed, at first, that she was Vigram\u8217\'92s slave. Her robe was very plain and spun from a host of earthy threads, browns and reds, waste-material, together affecting a dark russet. But the skill with which her long sleeves were woven said otherwise. The comfort with which she wore the piece suggested it had never been slept in. Then there was the matter of the very, very deep neckline, which was too sultry, as well as all the accenting jewelery, which was too heretical. Too much individuality for a slave. And Vigram would never stare at a slave like he was about stamp a return on interest.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Isn\u8217\'92t she a subject fit for holy oils?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked, squeezing out a suggestive smile.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Undoubtedly,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, and rare for him, he meant it.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93She is the Lady Pel,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93I should mention that she is interested in becoming your patroness, so be on your best behavior.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Pleased to meet you,\u8221\'94 Pel said, voice stern. She held out her arm, exposing her wrist. A thin silver bracelet choked the softest flesh. Hand out, fingers down, her bejeweled ring glistened. There was a clear of expectation that it should be kissed. \u8220\'93Vigram\u8217\'92s told me everything about you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I doubt it,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. He took her hand and shook it. \u8220\'93For one thing, I don\u8217\'92t paint anymore, so if you\u8217\'92re wanting me to rough up some backwater temple icon, you\u8217\'92ll have to find someone else.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Backwater?\u8221\'94 Pel scoffed. She turned to Vigram. \u8220\'93Does he always express himself so cheaply?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram shrugged. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It is as I said\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the boy has no self control.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, really?\u8221\'94 Pel said flatly. \u8220\'93I did not know such untoward meanness could come so naturally to a man.\u8221\'94 She chuckled while she appraised Mandri\u8217\'92s entire being. \u8220\'93Usually, that meanness is only a mask to hide a black pit of shame. Does that describe you, Mandri? Please be honest: was your insult an attempt to distract me from seeing how empty you are inside?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s legs began to sweat. This wasn\u8217\'92t uncommon whenever a pretty women looked at him, but it had never come on so sudden. He didn\u8217\'92t know what to do, or say.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you a little bully?\u8221\'94 she asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Maybe,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, smiling. \u8220\'93I do feel compelled to insult you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel smirked. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You are fitting the mold. That is good.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes,\u8221\'94 Vigram added, seemingly confused. \u8220\'93Very good.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Good, in what way?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked. \u8220\'93Are you going to hire me to insult someone?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Not necessarily,\u8221\'94 Pel said as she sort of sashayed towards the stool in which she would strike a pose. \u8220\'93Set aside all that. For now, I will observe. Pretend that I am not here.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But I\u8217\'92m only here to teach. Vigram is the one who\u8217\'92ll be painting.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s smirk spread into a sardonic grin. \u8220\'93You can learn so much about person by watching them teach. Especially if the student is difficult.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am the ideal student,\u8221\'94 Vigram protested. \u8220\'93Aren\u8217\'92t I?\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri nodded.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So it is,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93Now, we should begin. But first\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 someone quiet that animal!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 An old, yellow headed ox was mooing down in the leech lake. It was angry at being stuck inside its stall, and also, at being bled to death. It mooed again. It bucked against its restraints, then gave a desperate, plaintive plea: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mrruuuuuu!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Silence that beast!\u8221\'94 Vigram roared. His leechmen scurried into action. \u8220\'93And you,\u8221\'94 Vigram said to Mandri, \u8220\'93help Pel onto her stool. I\u8217\'92ll ready the canvas and paint.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri sighed a sigh for the old ox. He wished he had the courage to moo like that. He privately resolved to never eat a Meskalimi leech again. Then he did what he was told and helped Pel up onto her high-legged stool. Half a finger later, Vigram picked up stick of soft charcoal, and the lesson began.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The first exploratory marks were always difficult. Every work of art must be built on a firm foundation; get it wrong and everything that comes after will be wrong as well. Unfortunately for Vigram, he had that all too common beginner\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s habit of refusing to use his god damned brain. He started drawing wherever his hand happened to land, and whatever happened next was up to Solraheen. The end result was that Pel\u8217\'92s head was half the size it needed to be. It was also too left-of-center. There\u8217\'92d be an awkward expanse behind her flowing hair.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hold on,\u8221\'94 said Mandri. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re moving too fast. Don\u8217\'92t think of this as a portrait\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 not yet. All we have right now is an oval, a rectangular canvas, and where that oval sits on that canvas. All you\u8217\'92re doing is putting an oval on a rectangle.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then do it. Think about, where\u8217\'92s the best place to put that oval? How big should it be? Remember, you have the whole canvas there.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ve told me all this before.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rubbed the marks away with his palm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stepped back.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He studied Pel.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stepped again to the canvas, then scratched another black oval exactly where the first had been.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is that better?\u8221\'94 he asked with all the awareness of a potted plant. \u8220\'93You think it needs to be bigger?\u8221\'94 He drew the oval again, but only slightly larger. From then on, every other mark he made was accompanied by a look back to Mandri for reassurance. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t look at me,\u8221\'94 said Mandri, frustrated. \u8220\'93Look at her.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But I need to know if the marks I make are correct.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93They\u8217\'92re never correct.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 There was a glimmer of understanding in Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eye, but just as soon as it came it faded. \u8220\'93If the mark is always wrong, then how could I ever move past it? I\u8217\'92ll be redrawing the same line over and over again.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You move on when you can\u8217\'92t stand to try anymore.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That sounds miserable.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It is,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, feeling understood. \u8220\'93You should be defeated by the time you\u8217\'92ve finished. I\u8217\'92ve always thought that you should never feel good about what you\u8217\'92re doing, because that means you\u8217\'92re not trying hard enough. Now, finish\u8230\'85finish the basic shapes, at least.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Alright.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91finished\u8217\'92 the \u8216\'91basic shapes\u8217\'92. He looked to Mandri for final approval.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s your paint,\u8221\'94 Mandri said with a shrug. \u8220\'93But you need to understand the importance of the drawing. You\u8217\'92re always drawing. Even when painting, you are drawing.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know,\u8221\'94 Vigram grumbled. \u8220\'93You talk about it all the time.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram made to redraw the too-large chin, but was interrupted by a loud, mournful ox bellow.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Damn it!\u8221\'94 Vigram cried, shaking his fist.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Please focus,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t get distracted. Let your men do their job.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If they were doing their job, I wouldn\u8217\'92t have heard that noise!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Please,\u8221\'94 Mandri repeated. \u8220\'93Focus.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram closed his eyes and took a deep breath. When he next looked upon his canvas, he was resolved: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m done drawing! I\u8217\'92m here to paint!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He tossed his charcoal over his shoulder and picked up his favorite brush. He dipped it into a bluish shade of bronze\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the color of the jaw of a jandri man who keeps a close shave\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and then he threw down the first splotches of color in a flurry. It was an affront to the senses. And Sol\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s light, that bentberry fiber canvas was innocent. Expensive, too, a weave coveted for its depth of feeling, for how it made the undertones blush. Assaulted by Vigram\u8217\'92s hand, those tones were bruised and near to bleeding. It was a very confused and angry slapping around.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri had to look away.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He glanced in Pel\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s direction.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The moment his eyes wandered down the depth of her neckline, the corner of her lip perked up. Mandri let his eyes linger, because why shouldn't he look? Why else would she wear that cut? Why would she douse herself in that lilac scent? Why bite that honeyed, aching lip? Why, if Solraheen Himself was not inciting him to stare, why did the soft shadows of the vines overhead frame her green eyes with the most magnificent golden light? A magical vesture indeed. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, stop flirting with my muse.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am not flirting,\u8221\'94 Mandri claimed. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m checking proportions.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes, and how are her proportions?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The old goat\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eyebrows jumped suggestively. Pel huffed in annoyance. The yellow headed ox weighed in with an oxen roar.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93MRRRRRUUUUUUUUUUUUU!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s it!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Below, in the leech lake, two leechmen tried to force the yellow-headed ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s snout into a bag of freeweed smoke. But the men were too skinny. The ox bucked them both, then broke its constraints and jumped its rail. The beast tore through the leech lake, kicking up waves of confused, copulating leeches. Seeing this, Mandri\u8217\'92s spirit soared.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Stop that ox!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted as he pointed with his loaded brush. \u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s a five silver-strings of leeches attached to that beast! If you don\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Mandri said firmly. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ll make a bad habit if you stop in the middle of the work.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t tell me what to do, boy! On my farm!?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Aren\u8217\'92t you rich enough already? Let it go.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram drew up in rage. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t ask me to let go of my principles. That, I will not do. That animal defies me!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Would you let it go if I bought it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eyes popped. \u8220\'93What?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll buy the ox off you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So that we can continue with the lesson.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nonsense.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m serious.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That decrepit thing?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Peace of mind is worth the spend.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you making fun of me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No. Maybe }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re judging me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93This isn\u8217\'92t about you, Vigram. Just take my money.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But you lead a meager existence as it is. It would halve your wage.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll be fine.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re serious?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri shrugged.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stroked his beard. He glared at Mandri with his puckered brow, no doubt weighing the prospect of easy money against his intense desire to dominate that ox.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He pulled his coinpurse from out of his robe and undid the drawstring. He pulled out a full silver string, untied a quarter of it, then gave Mandri half of that quarter. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93Your pay, minus the purchase. As for the ox, I will have to tear the leeches from it first. Now, if you will excuse me.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram stomped back towards the canvas and tossed his brush onto the palette, not caring that it rolled into a swatch of blue.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Wait, hold on,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93The whole point of this was to\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t worry, boy, our lesson is already finished as this matter requires my attention. You may leave whenever you wish.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 With that, Vigram marched down to the leech lakes to harry his servants. Two leechmen had been napping under a tree all this time. Vigram screamed at them until his bald head rumpled and turned red. But his screaming worked against him, for it stirred a few leeched cows and goats out of their drug induced reverie. Their horrid shrieks woke up others, who shrieked in turn, and now a cascade of doleful whinnies, bleats, snorts, and muleish hee-haws pricked the ear. Elevated into a rage which rivaled godly thunder, Vigram yelled right back at them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri picked up Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s dirty brush. He twirled its horse-hair head through the muddy colors of the palette. There was enough untouched pigment for at least four more of these awkward lessons. Very expensive. Almost cruel. It felt like he was killing something as he ran the brush through an untouched slug of yellow. He tskd his tongue, picked up a wooden shim, then moved to scrape that yellow back into its little clay jar.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I can see myself liking you,\u8221\'94 Pel said. Her statement was almost lost amidst the cacophony of animal screams.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Uhhh,\u8221\'94 Mandri muttered as he matched her gaze. \u8220\'93What?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You actually care for that animal\u8217\'92s suffering. I do, too.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Then why didn\u8217\'92t you buy it?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel slid off her stool. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Because I can see the bigger picture.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri considered the thought. Because of course, she was right\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 there were at least two hundred more animals still stuck in the water. And then, what other cruelties were playing out in the rest of this godforsaken world? Saving that ox was not the most efficient use of resources. Then again, what was?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel said, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I wonder if you did it out of shame. Vigram says that you care so little about yourself that you neglect your basic needs. I wonder if you believe that ox is better than you, and that it should live for a little while in your stead.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I just want some peace and quiet, that\u8217\'92s all.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I see,\u8221\'94 Pel said, intrigued. \u8220\'93It is settled, then. I will return here tomorrow morning. As should you. You will be given a task. If you perform well, you will never have to worry about money again.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I have plans tomorrow.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Pel grunted. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No, you don\u8217\'92t.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93How would you know?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Because I am a witch.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s legs were sweating fiercely now.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 It was time to leave. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 If only Pel\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s damned smirk, that witchy smirk, full of feminine wiles and dark amusement, didn\u8217\'92t root him to the spot.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 She touched his arm. She took his hand and stroked his wrist with a playful, rolling fingertip-tap. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Meet me here tomorrow morning,\u8221\'94 she said. \u8220\'93You do not want to make me upset, do you?\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 She towered over him, and her green eyes laid him bare. They were a lover\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eyes, or a murderer\u8217\'92s. It was difficult to say because there was a fine line between the two.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Uhhh, no,\u8221\'94 Mandri said as he retreated. \u8220\'93No. I\u8217\'92ll be here.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Good,\u8221\'94 she said, brusquely. \u8220\'93You may attend to your wanderings.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri half-laughed, half-nodded, then hurried down the patio\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s steps. He hurried down Vigram\u8217\'92s lane, which was the most terrifying lane because it was sandwiched between two leech lakes.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What about the ox!?\u8221\'94 Pel called.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri waved politely and kept walking. He stayed to the right because the lake on the left held leeches bigger than his arm. Instead of stalls penning in live animals, the banks of that lake were lined with bones. The lake\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s center was a constant swirl as hundreds of those monsters swarmed just under the water\u8217\'92s surface, bunch-crawling like caterpillars, slithering like eels, desperate to get in a taste of whatever corpse had bothered to drop in. And the moment Mandri grimaced, a round shape popped out of that writhing mass like a crab-trap buoy. It rotated around, revealing itself to be a severed head, somewhat fresh, and human. Close cropped hair. An upturned nose. A mouth open in a silent scream. A leech latched onto its cheek, and pulled it under.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nope!\u8221\'94 Mandri said to himself. \u8220\'93Nope, nope, nope,\u8221\'94 he repeated as he darted towards Vigram\u8217\'92s gate. Once onto the road, he quickened his pace. He didn\u8217\'92t feel out of reach until he crested the big hill that overlooked Vigram\u8217\'92s estate. Only then did he risk a look back.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram and his squad of leechmen were chasing the ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s pink rump as it bounded through the marshgrass. The ox, leeches and all, dove into a hedge. Vigram roared, because he could not follow. Meanwhile, Pel stood on the patio. She stared straight through the distance, right at Mandri. Her green eyes were as vivid as they\u8217\'92d been up close.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He pretended not to notice.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He walked all the way to Geem\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s and used his meager pay to buy half a bushel of burgeons. They were down-valley burgeons, decent stuff, but the waxy capsule leaves were liable to split. The insides would dry out before he could get to them in the ways that he wanted to. But, that was all Geem had, so he bought them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He continued along the road, stomping his way through the muddy wheel-ruts, slapping away the flies, humming nursery rhymes, trying anything to distract himself from overthinking the sight of that severed head. Because it was only a severed head. That\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s all it was! It might have never belonged to a body, or been a person. There\u8217\'92s no way of knowing, really. Anything was possible. Besides, a rich man like Vigram was sure to accumulate enemies alongside the rest of his possessions. What was one little head? People were dying all the time.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri thought about his barren farm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about relaxing under his tree.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He thought about sipping a milky hooch spiked through with burgeon juice.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He would like to escape into that hooch. It would be bliss.}}